{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_6c3242568590d355b8462ecfd29fb8f422b0078899d016f91ed7a9691eef3934", "title": "Stand and Deliver", "text": "Stand and Deliver is a 1988 American drama film based on the true story of high school math teacher Jaime Escalante. For portraying Escalante, Edward James Olmos was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor at the 61st Academy Awards. The film was added to the National Film Registry of the Library of Congress in 2011.", "score": 24.2412}, {"id": "hp_doc_f4bb12c81940cab97c5ec90f26dc48e8d5807e36ce339721f34fe97ceb4c4786", "title": "Edward James Olmos", "text": "Edward James Olmos (born February 24, 1947) is an American actor and director. Among his most memorable roles are William Adama in the re-imagined \"Battlestar Galactica\", Lieutenant Martin \"Marty\" Castillo in \"Miami Vice\", teacher Jaime Escalante in \"Stand and Deliver\", patriarch Abraham Quintanilla, Jr. in the film \"Selena\", Detective Gaff in \"Blade Runner\", and narrator El Pachuco in both the stage and film versions of \"Zoot Suit\". In 1988, Olmos was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role for the film \"Stand and Deliver\".", "score": 18.0307}, {"id": "hp_doc_b615fff120e2b2219c6041a2486c659e622830434863ef59d346021e3bbd61e9", "title": "Heli (film)", "text": "Heli is a 2013 independent Mexican crime drama film directed by Amat Escalante and produced by Jaime Romandía. Featuring newcomers Armando Espitia, Andrea Vergara, Linda González, and Juan Eduardo Palacios, the film premiered in competition for the Palme d'Or at the 2013 Cannes Film Festival. Escalante won the Best Director award at the ceremony. While being appreciative of the film's technical aspects, film critics were divided in their opinion of the film itself. \"Heli\" was selected to represent Mexico at the 86th Academy Awards for Best Foreign Language Film, but it was not nominated.", "score": 16.1762}], "remaining_searches": 2}
